{"id":"u-ae306678-b137-4174-ac05-3311bfe83b6b","src":"community","title":"PULP: Periodized Upper Lower Push Pull","author":"Mohammed A.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/i6vZDg-upper-lower-push-pull","desc":"The PULP Program is a 12-week science-based hypertrophy program built around the Upper-Lower-Push-Pull split, designed for novice and intermediate lifters who want to maximize muscle growth while building a balanced, proportionate physique.                                                       \n\nPULP integrates Block Periodization, RIR-based progression, and strategic intensity techniques to drive continuous progress across the full 12-week cycle.                             \n\nWHAT IS PULP?\nPULP is structured around two training blocks separated by a deload week. Each major muscle is trained 2x/week, with priority muscles (side delts) hit 3x/week.                                           \n\nCore principles:\n1. Block Periodization: Block 1 (Weeks 1-6) for volume accumulation, Block 2 (Weeks 8-12) for intensification.\n2. RIR Progression: Reps in Reserve tightens from RIR 2 in Week 1 to RIR 0 by peak weeks.\n3. Intensity Techniques: Block 2 adds lengthened partials, drop sets, myo-reps, and static holds on the final set of select exercises.\n                                           \nWHY USE PULP?\n1. Priority Muscle Volume: Arms, side delts, chest, and lats receive 8-10+ weekly sets for targeted aesthetic growth.\n2. Trackable Progression: Same exercises all 12 weeks for precise tracking of strength and rep improvements.\n3. Joint-Friendly Selection: Machine-heavy and cable-based exercises prioritize elbow and knee health.\n4. Science-Based: Intensity techniques applied by biomechanics — stretch-loaded exercises get partials, metabolic stress exercises get myo-reps.\n                                 \nSCHEDULE (4 days/week):\nDay 1 – Upper: Chest + back compounds, arm + delt accessories\nDay 2 – Lower: Quads + Hamstrings + Glutes + Calves\nDay 3 – Push: Chest + Triceps + Side Delts\nDay 4 – Pull: Back + Biceps + Rear Delts + Side Delts + Forearms\nSessions run 45-60 minutes with supersets.\n                                     \nPROGRESSION\nDouble progression with RIR tightening. Once you hit the top of the rep range on all sets, increase the weight by the smallest increment and rebuild reps.\n                                \nBlock 1 (Weeks 1-6): RIR 2 → RIR 0 progression\nWeek 7: Deload — 50% effort, RIR 2-3\nBlock 2 (Weeks 8-12): RIR 1 → RIR 0 plus intensity techniques on last sets\n                               \nWHO IS PULP FOR?\nNovice and intermediate lifters with 6-12+ months of consistent training who want to maximize hypertrophy, build aesthetic muscle in priority areas, and train with structure. Requires familiarity with compound movements and access to a full gym.\n                           \nNUTRITION\nPULP works best in a slight surplus.\nCalories: Maintenance + 200-300 kcal/day\nProtein: 1.6-2.2 g/kg bodyweight\nFat: 0.8-1.2 g/kg bodyweight minimum\nCarbs: Fill remaining calories\n                              \nTarget 0.2-0.4% bodyweight gain per week using a 7-day weight average. Adjust by 50-100 kcal/day based on rate of gain.","level":["Novice","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":13,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-10-28T02:34:23.493Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Close Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"DB Incline Bench","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest-Supported Machine Row (Gym 80, Stack)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9},{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":10}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8},{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe